<!--
  sce:std/shared/record_join.scxml — what the host tells a copy of a shared record
  list (record_list) when it starts: the node id its stamps carry, and whether its host
  keeps a journal of what each change made.

  No copy is a hub: every copy sends its changes to one group every copy reads, and the
  layer below the list delivers them (docs/adr/0085, section 3.2), so a copy has no role
  of its own to be told. The flag that once named the hub is retired with the hub's
  relay; a key the schema does not declare is stepped over where the event is read, so a
  host that still sends it changes nothing.

  `journal`, added by the second revision, says whether the copy's host keeps a journal
  of what each change made (docs/adr/0083, docs/adr/0093). A copy that keeps one offers
  each change it closes to its host on the route `#journal` (record_list.made,
  record_made), takes it in only once the host gives it the verdict of the change's
  delivery layer (record_list.verdict), reports the outcome (record_list.closed,
  record_closed), and sends none of its own changes to a peer: its host gives what was
  offered to the layer that carries it. A join that does not carry it keeps a journal: a
  list a host starts keeps one unless it is told not to, and only a copy that is thrown
  away when its run ends (a scenario, a world run) is joined with `journal` false, which
  takes its own change in at once and sends it to `#people` itself.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:sce="http://sce.dev/ext"
       version="1.0"
       sce:kind="event-schema"
       name="record_join"
       sce:event-name="record_list.join"
       sce:revision="2">
  <datamodel>
    <data id="node" sce:type="uint64" sce:direction="in"/>
    <data id="journal" sce:type="bool" sce:direction="in" sce:since="2" sce:default="true"/>
  </datamodel>
</scxml>
